From 4b98e809100eea1afc1d912e5412ec028e4eb6bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm, skin.estuary: say when Dolby Vision goes out
 with the HDMI 1.4b signalling

Native output with the older signalling (the previous commits) cannot be checked from here: a TV
that does not take the HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame shows the tunnel as an RGB picture, with wrong
colours, and Kodi cannot know. So the user is told where it is used, and what to turn off:

- kodi.log, without debugging, when native output starts with it: "native Dolby Vision goes out
  with the older signalling, the HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame (HDMI_VIC n, given to nvidia-drm or
  made by the kernel), because "Dolby Vision with the older signalling (HDMI 1.4b)" is on (System >
  Display) and the display asks for it. Whether the TV takes it cannot be checked from here: if the
  TV shows wrong colours, turn that setting off";
- the Dolby Vision page of the player information: a row "Signalling: HDMI 1.4b vendor
  InfoFrame", after "Signal", only then (hades.dv.vsif is "hdmi14b" while the captured output sends
  it), in Estuary; the dialog that every other skin is given (system/hades) is made again from it
  by tools/hades-playerinfo/make-playerinfo.py in the next commit.

With the setting off nothing of this shows: the page and the log are as before, and [display-info]
still says "older signalling (HDMI 1.4b), not sent" for such a display (it reads the EDID, not the
setting). Strings in English, with es_ES, es_AR and es_MX (Estuary #31928 and #31929, used by no
other branch).

Checked on the host: the rows of the page in each state, with Estuary's font14, fit the panel (the
right column has 8 rows, down to 148 of 154) and every new text fits its 885 pixels in English and
Spanish (skin_check.py, with four states of this); the .po files are well
formed (po_check.py); syntax with the compile commands of the build. Not seen on a display.
